## 6b. D-2: z-conditioned neural policy (decision 2026-10-20)

{("Environment: the paper's ABM re-implemented in vectorised numpy (`src/collective_id/env.py`) so that arbitrary policies can be simulated; validated on the Fig 5B grid against the mesa ABM (tracking time r = %.3f, mean |Δ| = %.3f; pcr r = %.3f, mean |Δ| = %.2f points/s; the qualitative Fig 5B pattern is reproduced). Policy: shared MLP (2 × 64) mapping the paper's per-second features (tracking flag, detector, detector change, distance, with-social flag, #visible, signed social angle, social movement direction, social quality) plus the previous second's rotation state, and a 4-d participant embedding z, to P(no rotation), a truncated-Exponential magnitude and a direction probability. Trained per fold on the training participants' rotations only (%d–%d k seconds); held-out participants' z fitted on their own data with the network frozen (leave-one-group-out). Individual-level check (fit z on the first half, evaluate the second half, all seconds incl. zero mass): individual z improves held-out NLL over the population policy by %.3f nats/s (%.0f %% of participants; tracking seconds %.3f) — unlike the ABM-policy parameters of D-1, the learned z does generalise within person. Simulation: %s runs in %.0f min (100 seeds per group and variant)." % (EV.tracking_time_mesa.corr(EV.tracking_time_np), EV.d_tt.abs().mean(), EV.pcr_mesa.corr(EV.pcr_np), EV.d_pcr.abs().mean(), min(f["n_train_sec"] for f in F2["folds"].values()) // 1000, max(f["n_train_sec"] for f in F2["folds"].values()) // 1000, F2["heldout_gain_indiv_vs_pop"], 100 * F2["frac_indiv_better"], F2["heldout_gain_track"], f"{B2['n_runs']:,}", B2["wall_s"] / 60)) if D2 else "not run"}

